{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And two men remained.</b> In excess of the seventy." "<b>The name of the one Eldad and the name of the second Medad.</b> The elders were not specified by name, but these were specified by name, because the elders' prophecy ceased — it was from Moses' share, as HaShem said: ״ואצלתי מן הרוח אשר עליך״, but these had their prophecy from HaShem, as it is written: <b>and the spirit rested upon them</b> etc." "<b>And the spirit rested upon them.</b> Even though they were not chosen among the seventy, since they were worthy of it, they were not put to shame, and the spirit rested upon them and they prophesied." "<b>And they were among those written.</b> Rashi explained: he took seventy-two slips and wrote on seventy 'elder' and on two 'lot.' And if you ask: is there not great jealousy involved, such that the last ones could say that whoever takes first, by reasoning, each one might draw a slip of 'elder'; and since the slips of 'elder' outnumber the slips of 'lot' — one may answer: by the same reasoning, the seventy first ones could say: perhaps the two slips of 'lot' will reach our hands, since we are the majority, before they reach the hands of the last two, because they are the minority; and so it turns out that neither has advantage over the other." "<b>And they did not go out to the tent.</b> They did not go out from the camp of Israel to the Tent of Meeting with the others." "<b>And they prophesied in the camp.</b> About whom did they prophesy? About Gog and Magog, and their prophecy alluded to as it is written: כה אמר ה׳ האתה הוא אשר דברתי בימים קדמונים ביד הנבאים שנים — do not read שנים but שנים."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {3 "Reading ע״ב as ע״ב (72), following Rashi on this verse. The phrase 'פתקין של זקן יתרים על הפתקין של חלק' means the seventy 'elder' slips outnumber the two 'lot' slips.", 5 "The text of the cited verse appears garbled; it does not match the standard text of Ezekiel 38:17. Translated hyper-literally as it stands. The final play on words (שנים / שנים) works on the written form versus a re-reading, though the two forms are graphically identical here; the compiler cites a known midrashic reading of 'שנים' (two) as 'שנים' (years), referring back to בימים קדמונים."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:42.767784723Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}